; with T23DE:000A (two 4-bit pixels a byte), else T23FD:000A (a byte a
; pixel), both plane by plane from the plane of x, +0Ah/+0Ch added to x/y,
; the transparent value +8 not drawn, the base added to the rest; the far
; argument, when not 0, goes to T2515:0008 with the rectangle first (the
; background saved, presumably; not read). T258F:0002 gives the columns
; of each plane for a width. T0708's record of far pointers has it at +56.
; T2506:000A (x, y, base, entry far): a 'P' entry of 24x24 at x (a
; multiple of 4, presumably), the units (UNIT.LIB, base 20h for player 1
; and 30h for player 2 at the first map: a run, -vram, the sprites found
; in video memory as tools/libfiles.py decodes them).
; T24B5:000E (entry far): copies a 'U' entry of 24x24 as it is into video
; memory at DATA:0358 (in each plane 24 rows of 6 bytes at that address;
; DATA:0358 then moves 90h on),
; for copies through the latches, presumably (PART.LIB's terrain was
; found on the screen as decoded, base 0).
