; the texts (tools/txtfiles.py has the formats). DATA:0092 is a far
; pointer to DATA:00D6, a record the drawing routines take their
; arguments from: +0 the colour, +2, +4 x and y, +12h..+18h a rectangle
; (the clipping, presumably), +206h (DATA:02DC) a far pointer to the font
; of CHAR6.DAT, which T0708 loads (255 characters of six words).
; T2525:000A (x, y, text far): a text in that font, the pixels of the set
; bits in the colour DATA:00D6, 6 pixels on a character; 7Ch or 0Dh go to
; the next line (x as at first, y + 6), 0 ends. T2525:0082 draws a
; character: a row's word rotated by the plane of x, three nibbles as map
; masks through the table at T2525:0104 (the four bits reversed).
; T164D:0140 (x, y, n, colour): text n of GAME.TXT (the far pointer
; F27EE:4132, loaded by T0708): n texts skipped (each to a byte 2 and one
; more), then its lines, each ended by 0, with draw_chars, y + 6 a line.
; T164D:01DB (n, x, y): the number n in decimal with draw_chars.
; A run to the status screen (-vram): the texts 0Ah, 0Bh, 0Dh, 0Fh, 10h
; were in video memory pixel for pixel as txtfiles.py draws them, in
; colour 49h (AMOK's +0Dh), on both pages.
